WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.661 --> 00:00:14.089
Cut them down right here.

00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:15.702
You can see.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.560
My name is Leilani Kanaauao
Huggins, and I'm a lei maker.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.460
I grew up, actually, here in Los Angeles.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.820
I'm a fourth-generation lei maker,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.890
and I was raised in Hawaii till I was 6.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.760
My mom and my Hawaiian side of the family

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.540
just made sure I was immersed
in the Hawaiian culture,

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.600
and from a young age
I was making lei, and,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.850
like all cultures,

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.570
flowers are symbolic

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:45.500
of purity and celebration.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.480
You don't go anywhere
without giving a lei,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:52.010
without giving someone a part of you.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.370
You're giving a part of yourself.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.686
Traditionally, Hawaiian leis are

00:00:55.686 --> 00:00:58.170
woven with love and aloha,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.458
and the method used is just as important

00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:03.768
as the flower that's used.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:11.670
The ideal clipping is just
something that's beautiful,

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.500
that's not bruised or damaged

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.290
and that's not dried out yet.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.770
There's a few dried-out pieces here,

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.040
probably from the wind and the cold

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.490
that we've been having in LA.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.200
Mikala Jones-Fielder: It's,
like, very relaxing, too,

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.537
just finding the flowers.

00:01:25.537 --> 00:01:26.470
Leilani Kanaauao Huggins:
I call it flower therapy.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.230
Jones-Fielder: Flower therapy, I like it.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.260
Kanaauao Huggins: We sort of
clip it closer to the branch

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.590
so it promotes growth in that
we'll clean up these branches

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.150
when we get back to house.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.333
Jones-Fielder: So I picked this flower

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.500
because I'm learning from Leilani

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.600
that you wanna cut from the stem

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.590
and then we can do most of the work later,

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.340
but I thought this just
looked really pretty.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:54.460
Kanaauao Huggins: I think
most people will think of

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:59.070
that beautiful purple dendrobium
orchid leis as Hawaiian,

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:03.237
but those are made and
usually come from Thailand.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.820
Right now, there is a fungus

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:12.720
that is ravaging the
Big Island and Hawaii.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.750
It's called rapid ohia death,

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:19.750
and it's basically the
Metrosideros polymorpha plant.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.210
They're everywhere here in Los Angeles.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.640
In Hawaii, they're treasured.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.925
It is nice to have those

00:02:24.925 --> 00:02:27.930
because in Hawaii they're
not using them right now.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.600
Just real small lengths.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.173
We're gonna cut them down
right here, you can see.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:34.993
I'm gonna reach under you.

00:02:34.993 --> 00:02:35.940
This is gonna be the 'ōpala.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.350
So 'ōpala means trash.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.550
Jones-Fielder: I feel
like, when you're learning

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.583
how to make leis,

00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:42.480
you are also learning a lot
about the Hawaiian culture.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.772
Kanaauao Huggins: Yeah.

00:02:43.772 --> 00:02:46.012
Jones-Fielder: My lei
po'o. Did I say it right?

00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:46.994
Kanaauao Huggins: Yes, yes!

00:02:46.994 --> 00:02:47.827
Jones-Fielder: Yay!

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.160
This process is very relaxing,

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.540
educational, and just fun.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.490
It's very therapeutic.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.140
It feels very effortless,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:03.360
but knowing that I'm going
to create something with love

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.770
and give it with love is
just a really great feeling.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.610
Wow, the colors are so vivid.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.918
Kanaauao Huggins: Right,
that electric purple,

00:03:10.918 --> 00:03:12.218
it's so pretty.

00:03:12.218 --> 00:03:15.752
Jones-Fielder: It's gonna
look great on Instagram.

00:03:15.752 --> 00:03:17.032
Person offscreen: That's
the whole reason we do this.

00:03:17.032 --> 00:03:18.999
Jones-Fielder: Instagram
or it didn't happen.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.730
Man offscreen: Did you
both learn from her?

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:25.563
Delilah: Yes.

00:03:25.563 --> 00:03:28.004
Mariah: Yeah, she's
the master, lei master.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.513
Kanaauao Huggins: So we're gonna take

00:03:32.513 --> 00:03:33.590
a couple pieces of raffia,

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:34.650
some people use yarn,

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.540
you use kind of whatever you can get.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.940
So, we're gonna hili,

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.987
and we're just gonna make a
small slipknot towards the end.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.050
We're gonna wind our flowers all together

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.492
to make a lei like this.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.410
Leis symbolize love. It's yourself,

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.110
your giving of yourself,
your giving of your time.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.500
Your giving for birthdays,
for celebrations,

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.194
for anniversaries, for coming and going,

00:05:06.194 --> 00:05:08.911
you give it to show love
and respect and honor.

